{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"861700807626588220","content":"The trees and shrubs spent most of the night fixing up the park.  Instead of returning it to how it was, they decided to turn the damage into almost scars in the land, something to display, not hide.  They are proud of what they did last night.  the downed trees are turned into benches, the ponds refilled from the river.  Finally they take their place as silent sentinels of the park, forever ready to defend it from those that would harm this holy place.","created_at":"2021-08-26T12:18:52.283000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"880426068614467625","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"861700807626588220","content":"A fog rolls in, filling the parks borders, and it quickly rolls out.  A tent has been setup around the prisoners.  The side of the tent are the words \"Warden's Justice, Do Not Disturb.\"\n\nThe tent flap is drawn tightly closed.  After a while, fog rolls in once more, and when if leaves, those that surrendered are clothed in normal clothing, looking wide eyed.  The one that was a captain before stays behind, while the others quietly leave the park.","created_at":"2021-08-26T13:01:24.440000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"880436773136781373","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"861700807626588220","content":"_ _\nThe remaining man walks up to <@!443806147649208341> \"Thank you.  The others are banished from the wilds, but they were shown mercy.  The Chinnokin said as no arbiters have been set yet, it was his duty to pass judgement.  He showed us great mercy, but I was told that I cannot leave this park for one year.  In that time I am to defend my new home here, because it is on me to try to repair relations between the brothers that once called this city their home.  If you had not showed us mercy and allowed us to surrender, I would not be standing here today, a few blocks away from where I grew up.  Thank you.\" he bows before Ed, a few tears in his eyes, and he goes to walk off and look after the park.","created_at":"2021-08-26T13:07:33.271000Z","edited_at":"2021-08-26T13:07:42.061000Z","id":"880438320126111764","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
